      "content": "It's hard to attribute your experience directly to the market activity, although it's unlikely to be a mere coincidence. Your physiological response could have been influenced by a variety of factors unrelated to the market, such as an increase in adrenaline, stress, or even diet. Market volatility can indeed cause reactions, but correlation does not imply causation. It might be interesting to observe if this happens consistently, but take it in stride as an isolated incident without jumping to conclusions.",
