      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concept of a \"bio-network\" is speculative and not typically supported by evidence in financial markets. While it's interesting to theorize about subconscious connections, the timing of the market movements is highly unlikely to be caused by one's physiological state. Market movements are determined by complex global events and numerous factors. It would be more plausible to look for a coincidence in timing, but the complexity and scale of the market make it statistically improbable. It is possible that your body responds to the same external stressors that impact others, but this should not be seen as a personal link to the market's movements. Pay attention to your patterns but don't attribute your reactions to the market alone.",
